WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.620
Return to Monday,
January ninth, twenty twelve.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:04.890
At seven,

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.950
we ask for the hour beginning at eight.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.277
The saved hour and working day group
returns three hundred and forty nine point

00:00:13.277 --> 00:00:15.710
five zero rentals per hour.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.310
Now close the fitting process.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:23.500
A new process must produce the same
forecast without its old local variables

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.910
or training lists.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:30.280
The recorded outcome of four hundred and
twenty remains separate and becomes useful

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.730
afterward for evaluation.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.020
Reloading must preserve the
fitted function and its contract,

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:40.290
rather than reconstructing an
answer from a later observed count.

00:00:42.398 --> 00:00:46.238
The selected group is supported by
two hundred and forty eight training

00:00:46.238 --> 00:00:47.918
observations.

00:00:47.918 --> 00:00:51.788
Their outcomes sum to eighty six thousand,
six hundred and seventy seven.

00:00:52.478 --> 00:00:54.568
Dividing gives the saved mean,

00:00:54.998 --> 00:00:57.228
three hundred and forty
nine point five zero.

00:00:58.298 --> 00:01:01.808
This arithmetic explains where
the fitted value came from,

00:01:01.998 --> 00:01:05.568
but prediction does not repeat
the fit or read these targets.

00:01:06.118 --> 00:01:07.848
It looks up the stored value.

00:01:08.338 --> 00:01:10.378
The saved global training mean,

00:01:10.378 --> 00:01:12.958
about one hundred and forty
three point seven nine,

00:01:12.958 --> 00:01:17.508
is the simple baseline and
valid absent key fallback.

00:01:17.958 --> 00:01:22.488
Both levels retain rental units and
remain unrounded in the prediction API.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:29.990
The bundle gives the fitted values and
their surrounding meaning separate files.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.640
Model JSON keeps the original group bytes.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.950
Candidate JSON retains schema,

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:39.330
feature order,
raw output and fallback rules,

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:41.690
supported dates and known limitations.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:47.450
Calendar JSON supplies recorded
holiday flags without rental outcomes;

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.050
the manifest hashes all three
members and records their producer.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.010
The original review record is preserved,

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.970
while the later application receipt
records current execution evidence.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:04.110
Hashes establish identity rather
than trust in an unknown producer.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.970
A caller can pin a trusted manifest hash,

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:10.550
and semantic checks still
reject an incompatible schema.

00:02:12.668 --> 00:02:17.178
The constructor checks the bundle members
before making a predictor available.

00:02:17.948 --> 00:02:22.258
The target time is resolved
into a consistent hour, weekday,

00:02:22.768 --> 00:02:28.758
month, holiday and working day request,
with the issue exactly one hour earlier.

00:02:29.528 --> 00:02:32.938
Prediction checks that request
and looks up the saved key.

00:02:33.588 --> 00:02:37.058
It neither fits a transform
nor reads an outcome file.

00:02:37.588 --> 00:02:40.638
The selected group model
has no learned scaler,

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:45.068
but its forty five ordered calendar
positions still identify the input

00:02:45.068 --> 00:02:45.698
meanings.

00:02:46.388 --> 00:02:50.688
A request carrying an outcome or
an unsupported schema is rejected,

00:02:50.688 --> 00:02:54.418
rather than repaired by a
successful looking fallback.

00:02:56.648 --> 00:03:00.913
Change the requested hour to two in the
morning and the forecast becomes seven

00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:02.138
point five one.

00:03:02.728 --> 00:03:06.978
Change to a Sunday at eight and it
becomes seventy six point four three.

00:03:08.048 --> 00:03:12.154
A June Monday at eight still receives
three hundred and forty nine point five

00:03:12.154 --> 00:03:16.638
zero, because the function uses
only hour and working day status.

00:03:17.248 --> 00:03:20.638
Perfect reloading preserves
this lack of month sensitivity.

00:03:21.268 --> 00:03:22.898
It does not improve quality.

00:03:23.808 --> 00:03:26.038
All forty eight real groups are present;

00:03:26.548 --> 00:03:30.078
a separate small fixture
establishes the absent key fallback.

00:03:30.708 --> 00:03:33.518
Invalid inputs instead fail before lookup.

00:03:34.188 --> 00:03:36.198
Those behaviors belong to different cases.

00:03:38.483 --> 00:03:41.090
The preparation command
sends all four thousand,

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:46.223
three hundred and fifty seven validation
requests to a separate Python process

00:03:46.223 --> 00:03:48.233
launched from the run directory.

00:03:49.043 --> 00:03:51.653
Every result matches the
in process predictor,

00:03:52.063 --> 00:03:52.993
including support,

00:03:53.503 --> 00:03:54.913
fallback and identities.

00:03:55.923 --> 00:04:00.403
The independent audit also checks each
forecast against its original stored group

00:04:00.403 --> 00:04:00.913
value.

00:04:01.663 --> 00:04:06.253
An installed wheel predicts while all
access to the source checkout is denied.

00:04:07.003 --> 00:04:12.263
These checks establish a portable saved
prediction path rather than reliance on an

00:04:12.263 --> 00:04:13.633
old training process.

00:04:14.323 --> 00:04:16.933
They preserve the earlier
scores and failures.

00:04:17.463 --> 00:04:21.273
Whether those forecasts are useful is
still a separate empirical question.

